{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<pre><code>go get github.com/donseba/go-form/v2@v2.3.0</code></pre>
<p>Use the <code>/v2</code> import path. These examples target v2.3.0. The plain theme works without an external stylesheet; the default Bootstrap theme needs Bootstrap CSS.</p>
<h2>A complete rendering example</h2>
<pre><code>package main

import (
	"html/template"
	"log"
	"os"

	"github.com/donseba/go-form/v2"
)

type Contact struct {
	Name  string `name:"name" form:"input,text" label:"Name" required:"true"`
	Email string `name:"email" form:"input,email" label:"Email" required:"true"`
}

func main() {
	renderer := form.NewForm()
	renderer.SetTheme("plain")
	page := template.Must(template.New("contact").Funcs(renderer.FuncMap()).Parse(
		`{{"{{"}} form_render .Form .Errors }}`,
	))
	model := form.WithInfo(Contact{}, form.Info{
		Target: "/contacts", Method: "post", SubmitText: "Save contact",
	})
	if err := page.Execute(os.Stdout, map[string]any{
		"Form": model, "Errors": form.FieldErrors(nil),
	}); err != nil {
		log.Fatal(err)
	}
}</code></pre>
<p>This program prints HTML to standard output. It has no HTTP request or CSRF token. For a web form, keep the renderer, wrap the handler with its middleware, and use <code>WithRequestInfo</code> as shown in <a href="{{ basePath }}/submissions" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/submissions" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">handling submissions</a>.</p>
<h2>Register helpers once</h2>
<p><code>FuncMap()</code> supplies <code>form_render</code>, <code>form_render_localized</code> and <code>form_has_fields</code>. Configure the theme, translations, custom validators and store before concurrent requests start.</p>
</article>
